    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4840" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Băgōus</span></b> , i, and
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Băgōas</span></b> ,
			ae, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Βαγῶος</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Βαγώας</span>
		[Persian], <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a eunuch
				at the Persian court</i>: Bagou (<i>gen.</i> Gr.
			= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Βαγώου</span>), <i><span class="en">Plin. 13, 4,
				9, § 41</span></i>.—Form Bagoas, <i><span class="en">Quint. 5,
				12, 21</span></i>.—Hence, <i>any guard of
				women</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. Am. 2, 2, 1</span></i>.</div>
